{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Module migrations (U1, U2, U7) will be performed by copying code from XD to s-c-s/XD proper and then refactoring it to align with the new binder/channel model rather than doing a pure verbatim copy.",
    "Multi-binder support (U3) will be implemented via a binder-type-aware channel abstraction that allows the source and sink sides of a module to bind to independent binder implementations (e.g., rabbit + kafka).",
    "External configuration overrides (U4) will leverage Spring's PropertySource / Environment mechanism, allowing files outside the classpath to override module defaults and even module resolution coordinates.",
    "CC SPI deployer refactoring (U5) will adopt the Cloud Foundry Java Client API (reactor-based) in place of the older REST template-based implementation to improve non-blocking performance and design clarity.",
    "Hadoop distribution selection (U6) will be exposed as a configuration/CLI option that resolves to the correct classpath/hadoop libraries at CP launch time.",
    "Dependency upgrade (U8) will be done in a single coordinated change (SI 4.2, Spring 4.2.1, AMQP 1.5) to minimize churn, with all consumer code updated in one pass.",
    "Each migrated/added feature is assumed to ship with unit tests and at least one integration/smoke test, with effort included in the per-activity estimates rather than as a separate QA activity."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Effort is expressed in person-workdays of 8 productive hours for a single experienced Java/Spring developer who is also the implementer.",
    "Source code from Spring XD and modules repos is available, and the target repos (s-c-s, s-c-d) already exist with baseline build infrastructure (Maven, CI) in place.",
    "No major architectural discoveries are made during implementation that would invalidate the WBS; estimates are most-likely, not worst-case.",
    "Dependency upgrade (U8) assumes compatible APIs from SI 4.2 / Spring 4.2.1 / AMQP 1.5; only straightforward migration tweaks are required, not a re-architecture.",
    "Maven coordinates, package naming, and module identifiers may be adjusted to match the new repos without counting as separate re-implementation work.",
    "Hadoop distribution selection (U6) is a configuration/loader change, not a full rewrite of hdfs/hdfs-sink modules.",
    "Documentation updates are folded into the relevant feature activities plus a final pass; no separate large documentation project is assumed.",
    "No production hardening (extensive performance benchmarking, security review, multi-OS verification) beyond smoke/integration testing is included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and design",
      "activity_description": "Review the 8 user stories, study the XD modules and s-c-s/s-c-d target architecture, and produce a short design covering the new channel/binder abstraction, external config flow, CF java-client integration, Hadoop distribution loader, and dependency upgrade plan."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Migrate kafka module from XD to s-c-s (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Move the kafka module source and tests from XD/modules to the s-c-s repository, adapt it to the new module/channel/binder programming model, ensure it can be used as a sink, and validate with build and integration tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Migrate rabbit module from XD to s-c-s (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Move the rabbit module source and tests from XD/modules to the s-c-s repository, adapt it to the new module/channel/binder programming model, ensure it can be used as a sink, and validate with build and integration tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement multi-binder support for module channels (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the ability to specify different binder types per module channel so rabbit, redis, or kafka can be plugged in independently as source or sink, including configuration metadata, channel binding logic, and tests covering mixed-binder scenarios."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Add external configuration file overrides (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement support for loading an external configuration file that can override default module options (including module resolution from a different Maven coordinate), wire it into the module deployment/bootstrap flow, and test override precedence and coordinate override cases."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Refactor CC SPI deployer with CF java-client (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Replace the existing CC SPI deployer implementation with one based on the Cloud Foundry Java Client (reactor-based), improve the design/responsibilities of the deployer interface, tune for performance (non-blocking IO), and verify behavior with integration tests against a CF target."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Add Hadoop distribution selection option (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a configuration/option that lets the user choose which Hadoop distribution to load, ensure the correct Hadoop libraries are resolved at CP launch time, and document the supported distributions and selection mechanism."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Move header-enricher from modules repo to XD proper (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the header-enricher module from the modules repository into XD proper, update package paths, dependencies, and references, and verify it builds and runs in its new location."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Upgrade dependencies to SI 4.2, Spring 4.2.1, AMQP 1.5 (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Bump Spring Integration to 4.2, Spring Framework to 4.2.1, and AMQP to 1.5 in the relevant poms, update code for any breaking API changes, and run the build and test suite to confirm a clean upgrade."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing, documentation and release notes",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end integration tests across the migrated modules, multi-binder scenarios, external config, CF deployer and Hadoop distribution, update user-facing documentation for new options, and draft release notes covering the changes."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 35
  }
}
```

